{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And a man who takes his sister.</b> We derive from it ערות אחותך בת אביך או בת אמך and ערות בת אשת אביך. As is in Yevamot, chapter Keitzad." "<b>And she —</b> it is written with a yod (in והיא)." "<b>She sees his nakedness.</b> That both of them consented to this." "<b>It is a kindness.</b> In the binyan of יגיד עליו רשעו (he declares about him his wickedness) — both in masculine language, like פן יחסדך שומע." "<b>The nakedness of his sister he uncovered.</b> Under coercion, he bears his iniquity alone."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:50.291683422Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}